# Refined candidates - Phase 3 iterative mutation
# Mutating top 3 homogeneity candidates from batch 1
# Strategy: Add Fluorine atoms (salt reduction) and Double Bonds (polymerization)

# === Top 3 Homogeneity Candidates - Mutated ===

# 1. Mutated from COC(=O)OC(F)=C(F)C(F)(F)F (homog=12.29)
# Added extra F to enhance salt reduction pathway
COC(=O)OC(F)=C(F)C(F)(F)C(F)(F)F

# 2. Mutated from N#CC(F)S(=O)(=O)C (homog=12.28)
# Added double bond for polymerization + extra F for salt reduction
N#CC(F)=C(F)S(=O)(=O)C(F)=CF2

# 3. Mutated from FCC(F)(F)S(=O)(=O)OC=C (homog=12.26)
# Added extra F atoms and additional double bond
FCC(F)(F)S(=O)(=O)OC(F)=CF2

# === Conservative Novelty Batch (Standard carbonates with single-atom substitutions) ===

# EC with single fluorine substitution
COC(=O)OCC(F)F

# DMC with methyl-fluoro substitution
CCOC(=O)OC(F)F

# EMC with fluorine substitution
CCOC(=O)OCC(F)F

# Perfluoro-ethyl carbonate
COC(=O)OC(F)(F)C(F)(F)F

# Fluoro-vinyl carbonate
COC(=O)OC=C(F)F

# Trifluoro-methyl carbonate
COC(=O)OC(F)(F)F

# Difluoro-isopropyl carbonate
COC(=O)OC(C)(F)F

# Fluoro-ethyl methyl carbonate (verified)
COC(=O)OC(F)F

# Trifluoro-ethyl ethyl carbonate
CCOC(=O)OC(F)(F)F

# Vinyl fluoride carbonate
COC(=O)OC(F)=CF2

# 2,2,2-Trifluoroethyl acetate (carbonate analog)
CC(=O)OC(F)(F)F
